` read its `[verify]` settings from the project config committed on `origin/main`, never from the change under review. `docs/llm-framework.md` (the \"Trust model\" paragraph, around line 1063) still says the trust list lives \"in the verifying environment's own `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` (never in the repository, ADR 0125)\". It does not mention that the merge gate's project layer comes from main, so a reader of that page gets an incomplete, and for a repository-set list contradictory, account of where the gate's trust comes from. `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md` and `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` were updated in that change; this page was missed.\n\n## Approach\n\nAmend the one sentence in that paragraph so it states both facts: the trust list belongs in the verifying environment's own configuration (ADR 0125), and when the merge gate runs, its `[verify]` settings and `tracker.dir` come from the project config committed on `origin/main`, never from the checkout under review, so a change cannot widen its own gate run. Keep the rest of the paragraph unchanged. Wording matches `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (the op-cert quote block) so the 2 pages agree.\n\nDocumentation only: no code, config key, env var or flag changes, so there is no new testable behaviour.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/llm-framework.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The \"Trust model\" paragraph of `docs/llm-framework.md` states that `rebar verify-opcert` reads its `[verify]` settings from the project config committed on `origin/main`, not from the checkout under review: `grep -n \"committed on \\`origin/main\\`\" docs/llm-framework.md` prints a line in that paragraph.\n- [ ] The paragraph still says the trust list belongs to the verifying environment (ADR 0125): `grep -n \"verifying environment's own\" docs/llm-framework.md` still matches.\n- [ ] The docs gates pass: `pytest tests -k \"docs\" -q` and `make lint` exit 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"state the main-branch gate trust rule"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4ef0d40b-939e-4b9d-a167-cb20b8872b3f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"751c-9a76-cbd0-4007","ticket_type":"bug","title":"llm-framework trust model omits the main-branch gate rule","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["21c15b90-b086-49fc-95ef-9b4259b952ac","059eab98-77db-40f6-bc1f-147c94343a8b","85f29db1-fb22-431b-ae32-e02c32b10848","72134463-7535-4192-ab42-ee73e92d0da6","4ef0d40b-939e-4b9d-a167-cb20b8872b3f","97ce0c57-46ae-4595-a310-ec1d3e8bff90"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795248554319784002,"uuid":"a4908f68-c3ea-4068-951b-6d0baaf1d27f"}